# Agent memory

This directory stores per-agent memory files. Each agent gets a subdirectory
with a `MEMORY.md` index and individual memory files.

## Memory types

- **`project_*`** — project-level decisions and knowledge (e.g., ordering decisions, design rationales)
- **`feedback_*`** — corrective feedback the agent received (e.g., "gloss attribution errors")

## How it works

When an agent is activated, its `MEMORY.md` is loaded into context. The index
links to individual memory files. When an agent makes a mistake, the
Orchestrator records it as a `feedback_*` memory. Next activation, the memory
loads and the error does not repeat.

This is not prompt optimization — it is the system accumulating immune memory.
